\date{2025-12-15T00:04:54Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Some examples of things which are \em{not} [propositions](002P):}

\ul{
  \li{#{3 + 7}}
  \li{\em{Please hold this.}}
  \li{\em{Is the moon made of cheese?}}
}

\p{The first is an \em{expression} with a numeric value, not a
declarative true or false statement.  The second is a command, and the
third is a question.  The question could be \em{answered} by a
proposition (\eg "The moon is made of cheese."), but it is not itself
a proposition.}
